# Line endings: LF in the repository and in every working tree.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, so without this file the
# answer is per-clone: a Windows tree reports unchanged files as modified, and
# a CRLF blob can be committed into a file the Linux and macOS boxes hold as
# LF. On 26 Aug 2026 a CRLF-only Cargo.toml blocked a fast-forward pull that
# had nothing to merge — this costs time long before it corrupts anything.
#
# eol=lf rather than a bare text=auto: normalising only the repository still
# leaves Windows checkouts CRLF, which is where the phantom-modified files
# come from.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries — the only non-text committed to these repos. Listed explicitly
# rather than trusting content sniffing.
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
